An 82586 ISA Ethernet card for the i386 machine.

Two boards, one chip.  hw/net/i82586.c is the Intel 82586 itself: the
initialisation handshake, the SCB command loop, the command unit and the
receive unit, working in a window of shared RAM the way the real part does.
hw/net/starlan10.c and hw/net/elink507.c are the AT&T StarLAN 10 and the
3Com 3C507 that wrap it, and differ only in the handful of I/O registers the
driver probes them through.

The register and structure layout is NetBSD's sys/dev/ic/i82586reg.h, which is
also what the Wish82586 RTL is checked against; the point of the exercise is
that an unmodified vintage driver cannot tell the two apart.

Use the 3C507: NetBSD's ai(4) cannot attach on a modern kernel, because
ai_find_mem_size() hands check_ie_present() the ISA physical address where a
bus_space handle is wanted and the probe page faults.  ef(4) is clean, reads
its ethernet address off the card, and sits on the same
sys/dev/ic/i82586.c core.

  -netdev user,id=n0 -device isa-3c507,netdev=n0

